.TH PSOuterProduct 3 2024-01-03 "PsyC 0.9.4" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSOuterProduct\fR

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSOuterProduct\fR(\fIPSFloat *a\fR, \fIPSFloat *b\fR, \fIPSFloat *dest\fR, \fIuint64_t alen\fR, \fIuint64_t blen\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Multiply every element of vector \fIa\fR (having \fIalen\fR length) by every element of vector \fIb\fR (having \fIblen\fR length) and store results into vector \fIdest\fR (whose length must be the product of \fIalen\fR by \fIblen\fR).
.br
The function can take advantage of the available accelerations (both hardwware and software). By default, accelerations set in \fIPSGlobalAcceleration\fR are used, if any. However, the used accelerations methods can be changed via the \fIacceleration\fR member of the optional argument \fIopts\fR.
.br
Aside from acceleration, \fIopts\fR can also be used to set the result storage mode (by using the \fIstore_mode\fR member):
.br

.RS 4
.TP
.B PS_STORE_MODE_ADD
the result is added to the existing values of \fIdest\fR.
.br

.TP
.B PS_STORE_MODE_SUB
the result is subtracted from the existing values    of \fIdest\fR.
.RE
.RE


.SH RETURN VALUES
1 is the function succeeds or zero if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fIa\fR is \fINULL\fR or \fIb\fR is \fINULL\fR or \fIdest\fR is \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] BLAS computation error if BLAS acceleration is used.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
